" Possibly round to some precision? The fixture doesn't specify rounding. I'll use float as computed. However, the schema requires number, so float is fine.\n\nImplementation: iterate over calls, compute normalized_gain, check parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold, build diagnostics list and accepted list.\n\nEdge cases: threshold may be 0.05. Use >= (inclusive). The output schema requires accepted_call_ids and diagnostics. All keys required.\n\nWrite the Python code. Use only standard library.\n\nReturn the implementation as JSON string with key \"implementation\".\n\nLet's produce the JSON.\n\nImplementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case['threshold']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    accepted = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call['call_id']\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\n        parseable = call['parseable']\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        is_accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        if is_accepted:\n            accepted.append(call_id)\n        diagnostics.append({\n            'accepted': is_accepted,\n            'call_id': call_id,\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\n        })\n    return {\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted,\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nWe must ensure no mutation of case, but we're just reading.\n\nNow encode as JSON string. The entire response must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value being the Python source as a string.\n\nWe'll output the JSON.\n\nNote: The spec says \"Do not use Markdown code fences. Do not add a preamble, explanation, or trailing text.\" So just the JSON object.\n\nLet's generate the JSON. We'll need to escape newlines and quotes in the Python source. We'll do it manually or with a simple approach. I'll write the JSO